  "notes": "Darkchild's principal canvas: stacked-harmony R&B over syncopated MPC programming, 1994–2004. The research gives \"67–106 straight; 93 recurs\", so the mode is 93 and `halfTime` is false, and five sourced key/tempo pairs set the minor-leaning key weights. The three drum deltas are quoted: \"kick doubled on 16ths\" (4–6 hits a bar, syncopation 0.66, secondary anchor `2a`), \"snare on 2&4 with a 16th ghost before it\" (ghost probability 0.52 on `1a` and `3a`, the two 16ths that precede a backbeat), and \"hats in stuttered bursts\" (a non-continuous 16th lane with a high roll frequency and a velocity ramp). \"'Full Moon' adds a house-derived shuffle\" is why the swing sits at 0.56 rather than straight. Harmony is the sourced progression: \"'The Boy Is Mine' is `iv–i` (F♯m9–C♯m9) in C♯ minor across 32 bars\" — so `iv–i` is the top-weighted family and the ninth share is the highest in the batch at 0.48, with the triad share cut to 0.1. \"A keyboard harp patch as the intro hook and a cello countermelody entering before the chorus\" is the bell timbre hint and the counter at −12 sharing weight between `sustain_pad` and `answer_lick`. The low end is \"MPC-triggered 808 bass tuned to the chord root, short decay, articulated in 16ths rather than sustained\" — articulated and non-sustaining is bass-part behaviour, so it is the `bassline` block on `mirror_kick` and there is deliberately no `drums.bass808` block, which would have silenced it. ⚠ The INFERRED parameters are the velocity and density numbers, `swing.amount` 0.56 and the melody register; the research gives gear, key and progression, not a kit.",
